      'The best correction is to slow down for one move, not to inspect every possible order. Most levels reveal at least one clear route if you read the directions carefully. If you reach a point where every visible path seems blocked, use the path preview and check whether an arrow is pointing toward a blocker from the opposite side. A fresh scan after a short pause often exposes the dependency you missed.',
      '## Keep practising',
      'A few short levels teach the visual language of the game: arrowhead, travel line, obstacle and safe exit. Once those are familiar, you can think about dependencies instead of decoding every piece from scratch. For another kind of spatial planning, try [Traffic Escape](/games/traffic). If you prefer paths that you draw rather than arrows you launch, [Color Connect](/games/connect) gives you a different board puzzle. You can also browse the site’s [free online puzzle games](/blogs/best-free-online-puzzle-games) to find a style that suits your break.',
